{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>He sends, and they melt</b> — the snow and the frost and the ice. וישב רוחו is from the heavy [qal] binyan [i.e., pa'al], like רוח יהוה נשבה בי, from the light binyan [i.e., nif'al]."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 147, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra is analyzing the grammatical form of וישב (referring back to ישלח דברו in v. 15 and the melting in v. 18); he distinguishes qal passive from nif'al forms of the root נשב."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:05.644067098Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}